# Membro — environment keys. Copy to .env (git-ignored) and fill in.
# Both keys are OPTIONAL but recommended; start.sh loads .env automatically and
# prints exactly what degrades when a key is absent.

# Enables the utility model used for fact mining (POST /v1/distill) and summary
# regeneration (POST /v1/summary/regenerate). The default miner_model is
# claude-haiku, which routes through Anthropic. Without any utility-model key,
# those two operations fail loudly (nothing else breaks).
#ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# Enables embeddings (text-embedding-3-small) for semantic recall in /v1/recall.
# Without it, recall degrades to keyword-only matching. Also required instead of
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY if you point miner_model at an OpenAI model in config.json.
#OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# Your owner secret — worth setting even on a purely local install. It does
# three jobs:
#  - Recovery secret for the admin UI at /: it proves you're the owner when you
#    first set your admin password, and it's how you reset that password later.
#  - The `Authorization: Bearer` credential the optional read-only admin MCP
#    server (membro-admin) must send — it requires one even on loopback.
#  - Required to bind a non-loopback host (the server refuses to start
#    non-loopback without it).
# Leave it unset and everything still works, but the service mints a fresh
# random secret each run and prints it to its own terminal — so it changes on
# every restart and isn't a stable value you can hand to another tool.
# Use any long random string; to generate one:
#   python3 -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(32))"
#MEMORY_AUTH_TOKEN=

# Override the data directory (default: ./data inside the repo).
#MEMORY_DATA_DIR=

# Optional second-folder backup mirror. Every backup snapshot is also copied
# here, so point it somewhere that survives losing your main disk: an iCloud
# Drive / Dropbox / Google Drive folder, a second disk, or a NAS mount.
# Plain English: your memories are precious — keep a copy somewhere else.
# (Privacy note: a synced folder means your memory data goes to that cloud.)
#MEMORY_MIRROR_DIR=

# How often the running service takes a backup snapshot, in hours.
# Default 6. Snapshots are skipped when nothing changed. Set 0 to disable
# scheduled backups (a snapshot is still taken at every startup).
#MEMORY_BACKUP_INTERVAL_HOURS=6
